# Machine-readable citation metadata. GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this
# file, and the BibTeX block in README.md is the same record by hand -- keep the two in step, and
# bump `version` and `date-released` here as part of the release checklist.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If ordito is useful in your research, please cite it."
type: software
title: "ordito: GPU-accelerated triangular mesh processing on NVIDIA Warp"
abstract: >-
  ordito is a GPU-accelerated triangular mesh processing library built on NVIDIA Warp. It
  provides geometry, topology, repair, remeshing, spatial queries, discrete differential
  operators, geodesics, point-cloud reconstruction and registration as array-in / array-out
  functions that keep data resident on the device, with a trimesh-inspired API and a regression
  suite validating each function against established CPU reference implementations.
authors:
